caption: Body Plan and Features — Required
species-component: required-features

- SM -3; a typical adult weighs about 10 lbs.

- Feline Quadruped (Manual Forepaws) [-5]: Extra Legs (Four Legs) [5] and Horizontal [-10]. Unlike the published Quadruped meta-trait, this does not include No Fine Manipulators.

- Manual Forepaws [0]: The forepaws are ordinary fine manipulators. A Perfectly Normal Cat may pick up objects, operate tools, type, fire appropriately sized weapons, open containers, and otherwise use its paws as hands without a manipulation penalty merely for being a cat. The forepaws are not additional limbs; a forepaw being used as a hand is not simultaneously supporting quadrupedal locomotion. A cat using both forepaws normally sits, rears up, lies down, or otherwise braces itself.

- Articulate Speech [0]: Perfectly Normal Cats possess feline vocal anatomy capable of normal spoken language.

- Sapient Feline [0]: Their cognition is fully sapient rather than animal intelligence despite an otherwise ordinary feline nervous system.

- Domestic-cat physiology [0]: They have the ordinary dietary, respiratory, thermal, and other mundane biological requirements of domestic cats unless another purchased trait changes them.
